<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Fix a regular cardinal $\kappa $ as in $(2)$, and fix a morphism $f: X \rightarrow Z$ in $\calC $. We will give a functorial construction of the desired diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { &  Y \ar [dr]^{f''} &  \\ X \ar [ur]^{f'} \ar [rr]^{f} &  &  Z } \]
</div>
    <p>
       We define a transfinite sequence of objects 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  Y_0 \rightarrow Y_1 \rightarrow \ldots  \]
</div>
    <p>
       in $\calC _{/Z}$, indexed by ordinals smaller than $\kappa $. Let $Y_0 = X$, and let $Y_{\lambda } = \colim _{ \alpha < \lambda } Y_{\alpha }$ when $\lambda $ is a nonzero limit ordinal. For $i \in I$, let $F_ i: \calC _{/Z} \rightarrow \Set $ be the functor 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[ (T \rightarrow Z ) \mapsto \Hom _{\calC }( D_ i, Z) \times _{ \Hom _{\calC }(C_ i, Z)} \Hom _{\calC }(C_ i, T). \]
</div>
    <p>
       Supposing that $Y_{\alpha }$ has been defined, we define $Y_{\alpha +1}$ by the following pushout diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { \coprod _{i \in I, \eta \in F_ i(Y_{\alpha })} C_ i \ar [r] \ar [d] &  Y_{\alpha } \ar [d] \\ \coprod _{i \in I, \eta \in F_ i(Y_{\alpha })} D_ i \ar [r] &  Y_{\alpha +1}. } \]
</div>
    <p>
       We conclude by defining $Y$ to be $\colim _{\alpha < \kappa } Y_{\alpha }$. It is easy to check that this construction has the desired properties. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>